  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (Associate of Arts in Business, Bachelor of Arts in Accounting, Bachelor of Arts in Applied Behavioral Science); the Bachelor of Arts in Accounting was chosen because it is the only one with a complete requirement list. Please confirm this is the intended program.",
    "Associate of Arts in Business: the capture has no course list, and its graduation text names a different degree (Associate of Arts in Organizational Management).",
    "Bachelor of Arts in Applied Behavioral Science: the major list is cut off. Only 36 of the stated 42 major credits are captured.",
    "Listed components add up to 123 credits (33 + 54 + 36). The capture says 3 major credits may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements, and ECO 203 is marked as satisfying one, but it does not say which Foundations course ECO 203 replaces.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled first and satisfies 3 credits of elective requirements; it is assumed to count within the 36-credit elective block. Students with fewer than 30 transferable credits also take GEN 104, which satisfies 3 more elective credits.",
    "The capture does not list specific elective courses.",
    "Residency requirement: at least 30 credits must be completed at the University. The capture does not say which specific courses must be taken there.",
    "Upper-division requirement: at least 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major. Upper-division status is not flagged for individual courses.",
    "BUS 308 and BUS 401 require that the Quantitative Reasoning requirement be met first. The capture does not say which course satisfies Quantitative Reasoning.",
    "ACC 410 must be taken last in the program.",
    "The capture says Foundations courses may be substituted but gives no substitution rules."
  ],
